mod-acp-fix holds two kinds of files, under different terms.


1. The files of ACP: data/game/Interface/AddOns/ACP

These are files of the Addon Control Panel (ACP), version 3.3.4a, as the HD
client packs of World of Warcraft 3.3.5a carry it (Data\patch-5.MPQ), with the
changes this module makes to them (see README.md).

Their authors are probably sylvanaar, Rophy and Saien. This attribution rests
only on what the addon's own files say: its ACP.toc names "sylvanaar, Rophy,
Saien" as authors, and says ACP is based on rMCP, which is MCP modified by
Rophy, originally by Saien. This attribution may be inaccurate or incomplete:
the HD pack that carries this copy has changed it (its title reads "HD
client") and may have changed more, and no other source was checked.

These files remain the work of their authors and under their terms. This
module claims no right over them; only its own changes to them fall under
part 2.


